+---
+id: dl-005-createpatch-semantics-minimal-member-wise-diff-prefix-suffix-array-diff-no-move-copy
+type: decision-log
+title: "createPatch semantics: minimal member-wise diff, prefix/suffix array diff, no move/copy"
+status: pending
+---
+
+<!-- decision-log body. `wingfoil memory add` copies this scaffold verbatim; `memory submit` replaces
+     these placeholder comments with real content and fills the required frontmatter fields. -->
+
+# Context
+
+Clients want to send only what changed between two document versions, as a JSON Patch (RFC 6902).
+The patch must be small for small changes, must round-trip through `applyPatch`, and must not
+mutate its inputs.
+
+# Decision
+
+- Objects are diffed member by member (`remove`, then `add`/recurse in key order); equal values emit nothing.
+- Arrays skip the common leading and trailing elements, recurse index-wise on the middle, then
+  `remove`/`add` the length difference. This is cheap (linear) and gives one operation for an
+  append, insert or removal; it is not a minimal edit script (no LCS).
+- Only `add`, `remove` and `replace` are emitted; no `move`/`copy`/`test`.
+- Differing types or primitives give `replace`, with path `""` at the root.
+- Own members only, keys escaped per RFC 6901; values in the patch are deep clones.
+- Output is deterministic (insertion-order key iteration, no randomness).
+
+# Consequences
+
+- Reordered or heavily shifted arrays may give more operations than optimal, but always a correct patch.
+- Moves of objects are sent as remove + add.
